cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite both the article and this replication package."
title: "No Universal AI Dominance: replication package"
abstract: >-
  Replication package for "No Universal AI Dominance: A Multi-Dimensional
  Falsification Test of Vendor, Paradigm and Origin Dominance in Global LLM
  Adoption". States dominance as the null hypothesis and tests it on 61 data
  sources covering consumer attention, users, revenue, developer volume and
  enterprise spend, at the vendor, paradigm and origin levels. Contains every
  transcribed input, the analysis and figure scripts, an independent
  re-implementation of each statistical procedure, and a test suite that checks
  every number quoted in the manuscript.
type: software
